1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,293
They built a fire so large,

2
00:00:02,343 --> 00:00:05,846
the birds that flew over it fell from the sky.

3
00:00:05,896 --> 00:00:08,481
And into it, they threw one man...

4
00:00:08,531 --> 00:00:10,142
for the crime of saying:

5
00:00:10,192 --> 00:00:12,013
my Lord is Allah.

6
00:00:12,154 --> 00:00:13,172
But Allah said:

7
00:00:13,222 --> 00:00:17,225
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

8
00:00:17,738 --> 00:00:21,206
Who was this man, who stood alone against his father,

9
00:00:21,256 --> 00:00:23,321
his people, and a king?

10
00:00:23,404 --> 00:00:26,593
The man Allah Himself took as a friend.

11
00:00:26,643 --> 00:00:28,300
The father of the prophets.

12
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,322
The one who built the Kaaba.

13
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:36,127
This is the complete story of Prophet Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, from the Quran.

14
00:00:36,337 --> 00:00:37,798
The Friend of Allah.

15
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,059
Long ago, in a land of temples and statues,

16
00:00:42,109 --> 00:00:45,066
a boy grew up surrounded by idols.

17
00:00:45,116 --> 00:00:48,259
His people bowed to statues of stone and wood.

18
00:00:48,309 --> 00:00:49,733
They brought them food.

19
00:00:49,783 --> 00:00:53,659
They begged them for rain, for children, for wealth.

20
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,049
And his own father, Azar, worshipped them too.

21
00:00:57,259 --> 00:01:01,565
But the boy looked at the idols, and saw what they were:

22
00:01:01,648 --> 00:01:06,012
stone that could not hear, wood that could not see.

23
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:08,494
One day he said to his father:

24
00:01:08,544 --> 00:01:11,083
"Do you take idols as gods?

25
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:14,824
Indeed, I see you and your people in clear error."

26
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:17,204
It was a dangerous thing to say.

27
00:01:17,287 --> 00:01:20,511
In that land, the idols were not only worship.

28
00:01:20,561 --> 00:01:24,588
They were power, and trade, and the honour of every family.

29
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:29,092
But Allah had given this young man something no one around him had:

30
00:01:29,303 --> 00:01:34,177
sound judgement, and a heart that would not lie to itself.

31
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:37,475
His people also worshipped the sky:

32
00:01:37,525 --> 00:01:39,892
the stars, the moon, the sun.

33
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:42,862
So Ibrahim showed them, step by step,

34
00:01:42,912 --> 00:01:45,128
why none of these could be a god.

35
00:01:45,211 --> 00:01:48,400
When the night grew dark, he saw a star, and said:

36
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,269
this is my lord.

37
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:52,314
But when it set, he said:

38
00:01:52,397 --> 00:01:55,135
"I do not love those that disappear."

39
00:01:55,253 --> 00:01:59,338
Then he saw the moon rising, bright and full, and said:

40
00:01:59,398 --> 00:02:01,078
this is my lord.

41
00:02:01,128 --> 00:02:02,889
But when it set, he said:

42
00:02:02,939 --> 00:02:04,909
unless my Lord guides me,

43
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:08,254
I will surely be among those who go astray.

44
00:02:08,384 --> 00:02:11,993
Then the sun rose, the greatest light of all.

45
00:02:12,064 --> 00:02:15,453
This is my lord, he said, this is greater.

46
00:02:15,536 --> 00:02:19,574
But when the sun set too, he turned to his people and said:

47
00:02:19,715 --> 00:02:24,775
O my people, I am free from all that you associate with Allah.

48
00:02:24,986 --> 00:02:30,289
"Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth,

49
00:02:30,339 --> 00:02:32,332
inclining toward truth,

50
00:02:32,382 --> 00:02:36,177
and I am not of those who associate others with Allah."

51
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:39,379
Everything that rises... sets.

52
00:02:39,429 --> 00:02:43,003
Only the One who made them never disappears.

53
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,536
The hardest person to call to Allah was the one he loved most:

54
00:02:48,586 --> 00:02:50,070
his own father.

55
00:02:50,153 --> 00:02:52,566
And listen to how gently he spoke.

56
00:02:52,649 --> 00:02:56,976
"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear,

57
00:02:57,026 --> 00:03:01,181
and does not see, and will not benefit you at all?"

58
00:03:01,392 --> 00:03:02,503
O my father,

59
00:03:02,553 --> 00:03:05,730
knowledge has come to me that has not come to you.

60
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:09,285
So follow me, and I will guide you to an even path.

61
00:03:09,426 --> 00:03:10,247
O my father,

62
00:03:10,297 --> 00:03:14,229
I fear that a punishment from the Most Merciful will touch you.

63
00:03:14,279 --> 00:03:15,460
Four times he said:

64
00:03:15,510 --> 00:03:16,820
O my father.

65
00:03:16,961 --> 00:03:19,246
Not once did he raise his voice.

66
00:03:19,329 --> 00:03:20,846
But his father answered:

67
00:03:20,896 --> 00:03:24,074
"Have you no desire for my gods, O Ibrahim?

68
00:03:24,124 --> 00:03:27,116
If you do not stop, I will surely stone you.

69
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:29,869
So leave me, for a long time."

70
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,353
And Ibrahim said:

71
00:03:31,403 --> 00:03:33,107
"Peace be upon you.

72
00:03:33,157 --> 00:03:36,021
I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord.

73
00:03:36,071 --> 00:03:38,960
Indeed, He is ever gracious to me."

74
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:42,098
Words had not moved them.

75
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:44,850
So Ibrahim made a plan.

76
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,311
He asked his people:

77
00:03:46,361 --> 00:03:50,931
"What are these statues to which you are devoted?" They said:

78
00:03:50,981 --> 00:03:53,917
we found our fathers worshipping them.

79
00:03:54,058 --> 00:03:55,124
He said:

80
00:03:55,207 --> 00:03:58,549
you and your fathers have been in clear error.

81
00:03:58,632 --> 00:03:59,836
And he swore:

82
00:03:59,886 --> 00:04:04,412
by Allah, I will plan against your idols after you turn your backs.

83
00:04:04,553 --> 00:04:07,150
On a festival day, the whole town left.

84
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,776
The temple stood empty.

85
00:04:08,826 --> 00:04:11,227
And Ibrahim went in alone.

86
00:04:11,368 --> 00:04:14,557
He broke the idols into pieces, all of them...

87
00:04:14,607 --> 00:04:16,348
except the biggest one.

88
00:04:16,651 --> 00:04:19,283
When the people returned, they cried:

89
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:23,045
who has done this to our gods? Some said:

90
00:04:23,095 --> 00:04:25,251
we heard a young man speak of them.

91
00:04:25,301 --> 00:04:27,191
His name is Ibrahim.

92
00:04:27,274 --> 00:04:29,767
They brought him before everyone and asked:

93
00:04:29,817 --> 00:04:33,113
did you do this to our gods, O Ibrahim?

94
00:04:33,196 --> 00:04:33,889
He said:

95
00:04:33,939 --> 00:04:37,198
"Rather, this one, the biggest of them, did it.

96
00:04:37,248 --> 00:04:39,939
So ask them, if they can speak."

97
00:04:40,336 --> 00:04:43,318
For a moment, they looked at each other, and knew.

98
00:04:43,401 --> 00:04:45,965
Then they lowered their heads and said:

99
00:04:46,176 --> 00:04:49,215
you know very well that these do not speak.

100
00:04:49,299 --> 00:04:50,259
And he said:

101
00:04:50,309 --> 00:04:53,068
then do you worship, instead of Allah,

102
00:04:53,118 --> 00:04:55,948
what can neither benefit you nor harm you?

103
00:04:55,998 --> 00:04:58,805
Shame on you, and on what you worship.

104
00:04:58,946 --> 00:05:01,116
Will you not use reason?

105
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,846
They had lost the argument.

106
00:05:03,896 --> 00:05:05,739
So they turned to force.

107
00:05:05,789 --> 00:05:09,758
"Burn him, and support your gods, if you are to act."

108
00:05:09,841 --> 00:05:11,753
They gathered wood for days.

109
00:05:11,803 --> 00:05:14,957
They built a fire so great that no one could come near it,

110
00:05:15,007 --> 00:05:17,873
and they hurled him into it from far away.

111
00:05:18,014 --> 00:05:21,366
A young man, alone, falling into the flames.

112
00:05:21,416 --> 00:05:24,721
And then Allah gave the fire a single command:

113
00:05:24,771 --> 00:05:28,971
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

114
00:05:29,021 --> 00:05:31,200
The fire that was made to burn...

115
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:33,289
obeyed its Creator.

116
00:05:33,339 --> 00:05:36,076
It burned his ropes, and not him.

117
00:05:36,126 --> 00:05:41,384
"And they intended for him harm, but We made them the greatest losers."

118
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:45,732
News of the young man in the fire reached the king.

119
00:05:45,782 --> 00:05:47,601
He was a man so proud of his

120
00:05:47,651 --> 00:05:51,689
kingdom that he argued with Ibrahim about his Lord.

121
00:05:51,772 --> 00:05:53,092
Ibrahim said:

122
00:05:53,142 --> 00:05:57,158
my Lord is the One who gives life and causes death.

123
00:05:57,241 --> 00:05:58,305
The king said:

124
00:05:58,355 --> 00:06:00,627
I give life and cause death.

125
00:06:00,677 --> 00:06:03,799
I can pardon a man, or have him killed.

126
00:06:04,009 --> 00:06:05,689
So Ibrahim said:

127
00:06:05,739 --> 00:06:09,230
"Indeed, Allah brings up the sun from the east,

128
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:11,717
so bring it up from the west."

129
00:06:12,229 --> 00:06:15,165
And the disbeliever was left speechless.

130
00:06:15,248 --> 00:06:17,369
A king, with all his armies...

131
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:19,925
silenced by one sentence.

132
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:23,157
His father had rejected him.

133
00:06:23,207 --> 00:06:25,537
His people had tried to burn him.

134
00:06:25,587 --> 00:06:28,012
His king had become his enemy.

135
00:06:28,223 --> 00:06:30,321
Only a few believed in him.

136
00:06:30,371 --> 00:06:32,944
Among them was his nephew, Lut.

137
00:06:32,994 --> 00:06:37,971
So Ibrahim left the land of his birth, with nothing but his faith.

138
00:06:38,021 --> 00:06:38,761
He said:

139
00:06:38,811 --> 00:06:41,153
"Indeed, I will go to my Lord.

140
00:06:41,203 --> 00:06:42,711
He will guide me."

141
00:06:42,852 --> 00:06:46,830
He travelled for years, through deserts and foreign lands,

142
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:50,094
calling people to Allah wherever he went.

143
00:06:50,178 --> 00:06:53,529
And as he grew older, he made one more dua:

144
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:57,663
"My Lord, grant me a child from among the righteous."

145
00:06:57,713 --> 00:06:59,613
And Allah gave him good news:

146
00:06:59,663 --> 00:07:01,391
a forbearing boy.

147
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:05,302
His son Ismail was born.

148
00:07:05,513 --> 00:07:08,913
And then came a test that no father would choose.

149
00:07:09,054 --> 00:07:14,252
By Allah's command, Ibrahim brought the baby and his mother to a dry valley,

150
00:07:14,302 --> 00:07:18,108
with no water, no plants, and no people.

151
00:07:18,249 --> 00:07:20,302
The valley of Makkah.

152
00:07:20,385 --> 00:07:21,334
He left them there,

153
00:07:21,384 --> 00:07:24,436
with a bag of dates and a skin of water.

154
00:07:24,647 --> 00:07:27,383
As he walked away, the mother called after him:

155
00:07:27,433 --> 00:07:31,957
has Allah commanded you to do this? He said: yes.

156
00:07:32,007 --> 00:07:33,176
And she said:

157
00:07:33,226 --> 00:07:35,732
then He will not abandon us.

158
00:07:35,943 --> 00:07:39,411
And Ibrahim turned to the sky and prayed:

159
00:07:39,461 --> 00:07:46,841
"Our Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House,

160
00:07:46,891 --> 00:07:49,223
that they may establish prayer."

161
00:07:49,875 --> 00:07:53,784
When the water ran out, the mother ran between two hills,

162
00:07:53,834 --> 00:07:58,941
Safa and Marwa, seven times, searching for any sign of help.

163
00:07:59,082 --> 00:08:03,074
And at the baby's feet, water burst from the ground.

164
00:08:03,157 --> 00:08:05,477
The spring of Zamzam.

165
00:08:05,688 --> 00:08:07,555
It is still flowing today.

166
00:08:07,638 --> 00:08:11,570
Every pilgrim who walks between Safa and Marwa is

167
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:15,276
walking in the footsteps of a mother who trusted Allah.

168
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:19,725
Ibrahim had seen the fire turn cool.

169
00:08:19,775 --> 00:08:22,325
He had seen water rise from a desert.

170
00:08:22,375 --> 00:08:25,903
And still, he asked his Lord for one more thing.

171
00:08:26,207 --> 00:08:29,535
"My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead."

172
00:08:29,585 --> 00:08:30,580
Allah said:

173
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:32,414
have you not believed? He said:

174
00:08:32,464 --> 00:08:36,130
"Yes, but only that my heart may be satisfied."

175
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:40,913
So Allah told him to take four birds, cut them into pieces,

176
00:08:40,963 --> 00:08:43,411
and put a part of them on each hill.

177
00:08:43,807 --> 00:08:45,278
Then call them.

178
00:08:45,328 --> 00:08:46,370
He called...

179
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:50,435
and they came flying back to him, alive, in haste.

180
00:08:50,576 --> 00:08:52,999
Faith does not mean you never ask.

181
00:08:53,049 --> 00:08:56,426
It means you ask the One who has the answer.

182
00:08:57,430 --> 00:08:58,599
Years passed.

183
00:08:58,649 --> 00:09:03,117
Ismail grew into a boy who could walk and work beside his father.

184
00:09:03,328 --> 00:09:05,739
Then Ibrahim saw a dream.

185
00:09:05,789 --> 00:09:08,537
And the dreams of prophets are revelation.

186
00:09:08,587 --> 00:09:09,385
He said:

187
00:09:09,435 --> 00:09:10,731
"O my son,

188
00:09:10,781 --> 00:09:14,516
indeed I have seen in a dream that I sacrifice you.

189
00:09:14,566 --> 00:09:16,281
So see what you think."

190
00:09:16,331 --> 00:09:17,755
And the boy answered:

191
00:09:17,805 --> 00:09:20,727
"O my father, do as you are commanded.

192
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:24,258
You will find me, if Allah wills, of the patient."

193
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:29,017
When they had both submitted, and Ibrahim laid him down on his forehead...

194
00:09:29,067 --> 00:09:30,851
Allah called to him:

195
00:09:30,901 --> 00:09:34,336
O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision.

196
00:09:34,419 --> 00:09:37,424
Indeed, this was the clear trial.

197
00:09:37,507 --> 00:09:41,139
"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."

198
00:09:41,443 --> 00:09:46,747
Every Eid al-Adha, Muslims around the world remember this moment:

199
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:51,368
a father and a son who loved Allah more than anything.

200
00:09:52,370 --> 00:09:55,176
Ibrahim was now an old man.

201
00:09:55,226 --> 00:09:58,545
And his wife, Sarah, had never had a child.

202
00:09:58,663 --> 00:10:01,202
One day, guests arrived at his tent.

203
00:10:01,252 --> 00:10:06,451
Strangers, whom no one knew. They said: peace. He said: peace.

204
00:10:06,569 --> 00:10:09,526
Ibrahim was known for his generosity.

205
00:10:09,576 --> 00:10:11,906
Without a word, he went to his family,

206
00:10:11,956 --> 00:10:15,124
and came back with a fat roasted calf.

207
00:10:15,265 --> 00:10:17,223
He placed it near them and said:

208
00:10:17,273 --> 00:10:21,380
"Will you not eat?" But their hands did not reach for it.

209
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:23,251
And he felt afraid of them.

210
00:10:23,392 --> 00:10:23,888
They said:

211
00:10:23,938 --> 00:10:25,491
do not fear.

212
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:29,007
We are messengers, sent to the people of Lut.

213
00:10:29,057 --> 00:10:31,457
And they gave him good news.

214
00:10:31,507 --> 00:10:34,928
His wife, who was standing nearby, smiled.

215
00:10:34,978 --> 00:10:37,506
And they gave her the good news of a son,

216
00:10:37,556 --> 00:10:40,863
Ishaq, and after Ishaq, Yaqub.

217
00:10:41,004 --> 00:10:41,848
She said:

218
00:10:41,898 --> 00:10:44,240
shall I give birth, when I am an old woman,

219
00:10:44,290 --> 00:10:46,770
and my husband is an old man?

220
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:50,149
This is an amazing thing! They said:

221
00:10:50,199 --> 00:10:53,202
"Are you amazed at the decree of Allah?

222
00:10:53,252 --> 00:10:56,941
May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you,

223
00:10:56,991 --> 00:10:58,626
people of the house."

224
00:10:58,767 --> 00:11:03,978
From Ismail would come the Prophet Muhammad, sallallahu alayhi wa sallam.

225
00:11:04,282 --> 00:11:10,596
From Ishaq would come Yaqub, Yusuf, Musa, Dawud, Sulaiman and Isa.

226
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,779
The father of the prophets.

227
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:17,422
Then Allah showed Ibrahim the place of His House.

228
00:11:17,472 --> 00:11:20,082
And father and son began to build.

229
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,078
Ibrahim laid the stones.

230
00:11:22,128 --> 00:11:24,074
Ismail carried them.

231
00:11:24,124 --> 00:11:27,768
And as the walls of the Kaaba rose, they prayed:

232
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:30,483
"Our Lord, accept this from us.

233
00:11:30,533 --> 00:11:33,875
Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing."

234
00:11:34,155 --> 00:11:36,694
Our Lord, make us Muslims to You,

235
00:11:36,744 --> 00:11:39,680
and from our descendants a Muslim nation.

236
00:11:39,763 --> 00:11:43,360
Show us our rites, and accept our repentance.

237
00:11:43,664 --> 00:11:46,135
And they asked for one more thing:

238
00:11:46,218 --> 00:11:49,941
our Lord, send among them a messenger from themselves,

239
00:11:49,991 --> 00:11:52,729
who will recite Your verses to them.

240
00:11:52,801 --> 00:11:56,351
Thousands of years later, that dua was answered:

241
00:11:56,551 --> 00:12:00,717
Prophet Muhammad, sallallahu alayhi wa sallam.

242
00:12:00,788 --> 00:12:02,538
Then Allah commanded:

243
00:12:02,588 --> 00:12:05,220
"Proclaim to the people the Hajj.

244
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:07,286
They will come to you on foot,

245
00:12:07,336 --> 00:12:11,409
and on every lean camel, from every distant pass."

246
00:12:11,551 --> 00:12:13,254
And they still come.

247
00:12:13,304 --> 00:12:18,073
Millions of people every year, answering the call of Ibrahim.

248
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:23,443
In his old age, Ibrahim stood in the valley that had once been empty,

249
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:27,578
and he made a dua that Muslims still recite today.

250
00:12:27,708 --> 00:12:30,607
"My Lord, make this city secure,

251
00:12:30,657 --> 00:12:34,788
and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols."

252
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:36,516
Praise be to Allah,

253
00:12:36,566 --> 00:12:40,825
who gave me in my old age Ismail and Ishaq.

254
00:12:40,943 --> 00:12:43,832
Indeed, my Lord hears every prayer.

255
00:12:43,892 --> 00:12:49,243
"My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and from my descendants too.

256
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:52,097
Our Lord, and accept my dua."

257
00:12:52,147 --> 00:12:55,034
"Our Lord, forgive me, and my parents,

258
00:12:55,084 --> 00:12:59,099
and the believers, on the Day the account is established."

259
00:12:59,310 --> 00:13:02,232
Many of us say this dua in every prayer,

260
00:13:02,282 --> 00:13:04,335
at the end of our salah.

261
00:13:04,418 --> 00:13:09,896
The words of Ibrahim, still on our tongues, thousands of years later.

262
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:13,973
A boy among idols who would not bow.

263
00:13:14,023 --> 00:13:17,829
A son who spoke gently to a father who threatened him.

264
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:20,010
A young man in the fire.

265
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:22,379
A father in a dry valley.

266
00:13:22,429 --> 00:13:27,094
An old man laying stones for a House he would never see filled.

267
00:13:27,177 --> 00:13:29,242
Every time, he was alone.

268
00:13:29,325 --> 00:13:32,086
And every time, Allah was enough for him.

269
00:13:32,170 --> 00:13:33,385
Allah says:

270
00:13:33,435 --> 00:13:37,857
"There has already been for you an excellent example in Ibrahim."

271
00:13:37,998 --> 00:13:41,177
And Allah left his name in our prayers.

272
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,371
Every time we pray,

273
00:13:42,421 --> 00:13:46,540
we send blessings on Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim.

274
00:13:46,590 --> 00:13:49,177
"Peace upon Ibrahim."

275
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:53,389
If this story moved you, subscribe to Haq Stories.

276
00:13:53,439 --> 00:13:56,969
And watch the complete story of Prophet Musa next.
